{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>My rainbow.</b> It is a great sign, for it is, as it were, His likeness, as it is written: ״כמראה הקשת כן מראה דמות כבוד ה׳.״ And if My intention is to destroy — when the rains are heavy — I do not show you the likeness of My glory, for it is not the way of a king to come among his servants when they are reprimanded by Him. Another interpretation: why was the rainbow singled out to be given for all time more than other signs? Because the rainbow shows fire, shows water, shows red, shows green, and even though it shows water alongside fire, they do not extinguish the fire — so too the rainbow is a sign that the rains will no longer flood the world. Another interpretation: when the rainbow is seen, its nock is turned downward — this is the way of peace, for bowmen who seek to shoot aim the string toward their faces and the bow toward the enemies; but this bow has its string toward us."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:40.622569017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}